topic("pictograms","WHMIS pictograms — original course chart","whmis",[
  ["pict-flame","Flame — flammable and related fire hazards","The chart associates the flame with flammables and several related fire hazards, including self-heating materials. The flame-over-circle symbol separately identifies oxidizers, so the two must not be interchanged.",[20],"Which pictogram does the chart associate with flammables and self-heating materials?","The pictogram for flammables in the chart is a _____.","flame"],
  ["pict-oxidizer","Flame over circle — oxidizer","The flame-over-circle symbol identifies an oxidizer in the supplied chart. Its circle distinguishes it from the plain flame used for flammable and related hazards.",[20],"Which pictogram identifies oxidizers in the supplied chart?","The flame-over-circle pictogram identifies an _____.","oxidizer",["oxidiser"]],
  ["pict-bomb","Exploding bomb — explosive and severe reactive hazards","The chart associates the exploding bomb with explosive and severe self-reactive/organic-peroxide hazards. It is not the gas-cylinder symbol, which identifies gas under pressure.",[20],"Which chart symbol identifies explosive and severe reactive hazards?","The chart's explosive-hazard pictogram is an exploding _____.","bomb"],
  ["pict-cylinder","Gas cylinder — gas under pressure","The gas-cylinder symbol identifies gas under pressure. This is distinct from the flame symbol; a pressure hazard should not be interpreted as a claim that every such gas is flammable.",[20],"Which pictogram identifies gas under pressure?","The gas-cylinder pictogram identifies gas under _____.","pressure"],
  ["pict-corrosion","Corrosion — serious eye damage, skin corrosion or metal corrosion","The chart associates corrosion with serious eye damage, skin corrosion and corrosivity to metals. The exclamation mark instead includes irritant effects; those labels do not communicate the same severity/category.",[20],"Which chart symbol covers serious eye damage, skin corrosion and corrosion to metals?","The pictogram covering skin corrosion and corrosive effects on metals is _____.","corrosion"],
  ["pict-skull","Skull and crossbones — acute toxicity, fatal or toxic","The skull-and-crossbones symbol marks the fatal/toxic acute-toxicity category in this chart. The exclamation mark can also include harmful acute toxicity, so 'acute toxicity' alone does not make the two symbols interchangeable.",[20],"Which chart symbol identifies acute toxicity described as fatal or toxic?","The fatal/toxic acute-toxicity symbol is a _____ and crossbones.","skull"],
  ["pict-bio","Biohazard — biohazardous infectious materials","The chart labels the biohazard symbol for infectious materials. It is a different hazard category from chemical corrosion or gas pressure, so the symbol's actual meaning must be recognized.",[20],"Which chart symbol identifies biohazardous infectious materials?","The chart's biohazard symbol identifies biohazardous _____ materials.","infectious"],
  ["pict-health","Health hazard — cancer and other serious health effects","The silhouette health-hazard symbol includes carcinogenicity, respiratory sensitization and reproductive toxicity in the chart. It differs from the exclamation mark used for irritant and certain harmful effects.",[20],"Which chart symbol includes carcinogenicity and reproductive toxicity?","The chart's health-hazard symbol includes _____ toxicity.","reproductive"],
  ["pict-exclamation","Exclamation mark — irritant and certain harmful effects","The chart lists skin/eye irritation, skin sensitization and harmful acute toxicity under the exclamation mark. It should not replace the skull symbol when the chart specifically says fatal or toxic.",[20],"Which chart symbol includes skin/eye irritation and skin sensitization?","The pictogram listing skin/eye irritation is the _____ mark.","exclamation"],
  ["pict-environment","Environment — aquatic toxicity","The tree/fish environment symbol identifies aquatic toxicity in the chart. The chart also notes it is not required by WHMIS but may be used; it should not be taught as universally mandatory on every label.",[20],"Which chart symbol identifies aquatic toxicity?","The environment pictogram in the chart identifies _____ toxicity.","aquatic"],
]);
